The registry's agent-skills lintSuppressions array is a line-numbered mirror of these four .eta templates' front-config lintSuppressions blocks, which the compiler actually reads to suppress lint at build time; registry-reconciliation.test.ts checks only the aggregate count against lintSuppressionBudget, so a rule-name or line-range edit in one place that isn't mirrored in the other passes every test while becoming false documentation. Same pattern as voice-lint-suppression-anchors, applied to the agent-skills plugin's own suppressions (including the reference/helper-reference.md.eta ranges that plugins/agent-skills/scripts/sync-helper-reference.mjs regenerates).
